// ============================================================================
// MTP vertical line-shaft pumps -- performance data
//
// MSP Pumps & Motors manufactures this vertical range under licence. The
// licensor's VS and VG catalogue prefixes are both re-coded here to MSP's own
// MTP scheme. The two prefixes use disjoint series numbers (VS 30-260,
// VG 122-244), so collapsing them onto MTP introduced no new collisions --
// verified: 71 repeated model codes before the rename, the same 71 after.
//
// The catalogue publishes NUMERIC duty tables rather than curves, so these are
// parsed values, not digitised pixels. Every duty point carries absorbed power
// P (kW), which is what makes pump / motor / system efficiency computable at
// the duty point.
//
// SPEED CORRECTION. The catalogue prints the running speed as an
// "<n> RPM - T/MIN" header above each table; the spreadsheet extraction lost
// it and carried the speed down from the previous table. Speeds here were
// re-derived from the PDF by walking each page top to bottom and stamping each
// Ref with the last RPM header above it. All 1452 rows matched the catalogue
// on (ref, code); 298 speeds were wrong and are corrected. That fixed two
// things at once:
//   * the 134 rows that shared code + frequency + speed with a conflicting
//     row -- they were the same pump at two different speeds. Now 0.
//   * the 207 models with no frequency. Now 0.
// Checked independently against the affinity laws: of the 71 codes published
// at two speeds, all 71 scale as H ~ n^2 within 25%, none outside.
//
// Frequency is derived from speed: a speed just under a synchronous speed is
// mains-driven (980/1480/2900-2980 -> 50 Hz, 1180/1750-1780/3550-3570 ->
// 60 Hz); 2400/2600/2650 rpm match no pole count at either frequency and are
// engine speeds, marked "Engine". Every "Engine" row is diesel drive, and no
// electric model landed there.
//
// Entries are an ARRAY, not an object keyed by code: 71 codes repeat across
// speeds. Each entry joins Model_List to Performance_Data on (ref, code, rpm),
// which is exactly 1:1 -- all 8903 published duty points used once, none
// dropped or duplicated.
//
// Not yet captured: NPSH and efficiency curves, and dimensional drawings.
// ============================================================================

